e it if there's  one thing we've learned about Big Boss  and Solid Snake over the course of Metal  Gear Solid it's that they have some  pretty crazy dreams in Metal Gear Solid  3 big  who is referred to as Naked Snake at  this time is tortured and thrown in jail  yep jail again at this point you can  save the game and reload your file to  trigger a codec scene with one of your  contacts paramedic  she'll chat to you about horror movies  and after snake falls asleep he dreams  and a minigame called guy savage  launches in the game a character battles  zombies with two hooked blades until  time runs out  and that's when snake wakes up at one  point in Metal Gear Solid 4 a much older  Solid Snake takes a short helicopter nap  and we're given a chance to play through  his dream this time it's the opening  sequence to the first Metal Gear Solid  game in its PlayStation 1 forum judging  by his reaction when he wakes up he  probably has this dream a lot which is  pretty weird here probably heard this  one before but I'd be seriously remiss  not to mention Psycho Mantis and his  memory card reading ways in one of  gaming's coolest moments the telekinetic  Psycho Mantis shows Nick just what he's  made of  he uses his powers to move objects with  his mind by activating the controller's  rumble feature after you place it on the  ground and he reads your memory or more  accurately your PlayStation 1 memory  card and comments on any Konami games  you happen to have save files for with  phrases like I can see that you enjoy  Konami games you enjoy role-playing  games and you like Castlevania don't you  when he makes an appearance in Metal  Gear Solid 4 he tries to do it all again  that has a lot of trouble this time  around since the PlayStation 3 sixaxis  controller didn't have a rumble feature  at the time of the game's release and he  has trouble reading your memory card  since the ps3 had moved to a harddrive  based storage system boss battles in  Metal Gear Solid II usually 